## Summary

UX cleanup of the .pacnew review flow (frontend-only: main.js, style.css, JS contract
test). The Updates-view config notice is now a compact one-line banner (count + Review
button); all detail/warnings/per-file actions live only in the .pacnew center. The
center's mirrorlist row swaps the "Do not overwrite" prose for an "Open Mirror settings"
navigation button + "Keep your mirrors" label — deliberately navigation, not an inline
regen button, per docs/plans/2026-07-16-mirrorlist-regeneration-safety.md. Unused
config-notice CSS pruned. Also corrected stale docs found on arrival: the previous baton
recorded 31d17cf, but 68a7bd1 (TOCTOU-safe AUR install) and the 0.15.0 release (a49cb4b)
had landed undocumented; STATUS.md's Version line was stale at 0.14.0 → now 0.15.0.

Follow-up after Vatteck's GUI eyeball: the mirrorlist row still shouted (danger tone)
despite every remaining action being safe — pacnewRisk now returns info + "Safe to
discard" for it (danger level removed with its CSS), and tone-info rows keep the neutral
base border instead of the accent color (red accents made every row look like an alarm).

Then (same session): the transaction terminal got log syntax highlighting (pure
highlightLogLine in main.js; tlog-* classes mirroring pacman/makepkg terminal colors;
contract-tested) and moved from a right sidepane to a centered floating dialog (CSS-only,
same DOM/ids/watcher protocol). Plan: docs/plans/2026-07-17-terminal-highlight-popup.md.

Vatteck GUI-verified the highlighting + dialog. Their eyeball surfaced two polish bugs,
both fixed: the Updates banner ran full-bleed (now has the grid's 24px gutter), and the
install-preview dependency tree was visually broken — its CSS used an undefined
--color-success (green coding never rendered; border stubs fell back to white), rows were
double-indented, and every repo row had a noisy chip. Rebuilt as dot-coded rows (real
--status-* vars) + AUR-only chips + a legend; testRenderDepTree updated.

Then: startup-memory investigation (user report: "ate all RAM during initial indexing,
fine after"). Full baseline measured + recorded in
docs/plans/2026-07-17-memory-baseline.md — read it before touching memory (it records
dead ends: tracemalloc inflates RSS 3×, MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 is *worse*, malloc_trim ~1 MB).
Root cause found + fixed: map_desktop_files buffered `pacman -Ql <all pkgs>` (46 MB
here) as one string during the first-run disk-cache warm-up; now streamed
(atlas/gems/arch/pacman.py, +3 tests). Measured cold-run python peak 528.7 → 451.7 MB.
Then: shipped in-flight coalescing of concurrent full read_installed calls
(GenericSoftwareManager, leader/follower, ATLAS_NO_READ_COALESCING=1 kill switch,
5 tests; plan docs/plans/2026-07-17-coalesce-read-installed.md). Honest outcome recorded
in that plan: NO measured memory delta (GUI overlap is timing-dependent; benches ran
sequentially) — kept as a cheap guard. The remaining cold-start duplicate is structural
(GUI arch read waits on the pre-cacher's disk-cache task; the pre-cacher's own read
feeds that cache — circular-wait risk) and needs an arch-gem redesign plan before
touching.

**Verification:** all 773 tests pass. GUI eyeballs still wanted: banner gutters, rebuilt
dep tree (AUR install/update preview), calmed .pacnew center.
